{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527228779,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2NDU4ODMwMjc="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1527257033,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MjA2ODE3NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2553#issuecomment-392068174"},"message":"makes sense.  We should probably follow annex's suite and record \"discovered\" (in)capabilities within .git/config","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1543054537,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTk4NDk0MjYxMA=="},"added":[],"removed":["question"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1543055535,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTM1ODA4Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2553#issuecomment-441358086"},"message":"I wonder if it would be the simplest if we enhance ConfigManager to exec any callable that is passed via `default=` and store its result in the config, before giving it back. A callable can never come from `git config`, so there cannot be confusion.\n\nWhich callable (i.e. test) to run for any particular capability, could either come from a central library of tests, or could be specified ad-hoc for rare/unique cases. In both scenarios the config handling could/would be the same.\n\nGiven that capabilties could vary across datasets, we should probably give these test callables a mandatory dataset argument.\n\nHaving written that, we might just add a dedicated capability test method to ConfigManager and be done with it ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1543069552,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTM3MTY1MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2553#issuecomment-441371650"},"message":"Sounds reasonable. In some (many?) cases it would be the same underlying cmdline call (e.g. `git annex info`) which would provide multiple records at once.  It then might be \"suboptimal\" to call it over and over again for taking only parts of its output.  May be if such a callable could populate a set of config items at once? (if e.g. returns a dictionary)","files":null}]}